Let size be 3.
Let matrix be a list of 9 zeros.
Let visited be a list of 9 zeros.
Let row be 0.
Let column be 0.
Let down be 0.
Let right be 1.
Let counter be 1.
For every step from 0 to 8.
Set item (row times size plus column) of matrix to counter.
Set item (row times size plus column) of visited to 1.
Add 1 to counter.
Let next row be row plus down.
Let next column be column plus right.
Let blocked be 0.
Let old down be 0.
If next row is less than 0 or next row is at least size or next column is less than 0 or next column is at least size, set blocked to 1.
If blocked is 0 and item (next row times size plus next column) of visited is 1, set blocked to 1.
If blocked is 1, set old down to down.
If blocked is 1, set down to right.
If blocked is 1, set right to 0 minus old down.
Set row to row plus down.
Set column to column plus right.

For each value in matrix, print value.
